hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22680","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, Ibn Muhayriz narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Sa'di, a man of Banu Malik ibn Hanbal, that he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among people of his companions, so they said to him: Guard our saddles, then enter, and he was the youngest of the people. So he fulfilled their need for them, then they said to him: Enter. So he entered and said: My need. He said: My need, inform me, has migration ended? Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your need is better than their needs; migration does not cease as long as the enemy is fought."
